00:40:46.020 --> 00:40:47.680
can wear and gain strength

00:40:47.680 --> 00:40:50.130
and basically realize
that they can make it

00:40:50.130 --> 00:40:51.400
through whatever they're going through.

00:40:51.400 --> 00:40:53.050
- Okay.

00:40:53.050 --> 00:40:54.570
- [Liam] My question is

00:40:54.570 --> 00:40:56.420
I do want to eventually at some point

00:40:56.420 --> 00:40:58.410
be able to donate free clothes

00:40:58.410 --> 00:40:59.850
to these people.

00:40:59.850 --> 00:41:01.980
My concerns are that one,

00:41:01.980 --> 00:41:03.280
should I wait for my brand

00:41:03.280 --> 00:41:05.930
to actually be big
enough to mean something

00:41:05.930 --> 00:41:07.300
or should I just like cut the shit

00:41:07.300 --> 00:41:08.930
and start doing it now

00:41:08.930 --> 00:41:10.170
when it's not really built,

00:41:10.170 --> 00:41:11.560
doesn't really mean much?

00:41:11.560 --> 00:41:13.140
- If the punch line of the product

00:41:13.140 --> 00:41:15.310
is to inspire them and give them courage

00:41:15.310 --> 00:41:17.790
and you haven't established that brand,

00:41:17.790 --> 00:41:20.590
then you're just giving them clothes.

00:41:20.590 --> 00:41:22.280
So usually I'm a,

00:41:22.280 --> 00:41:24.670
as you can tell and you probably know,

00:41:24.670 --> 00:41:26.550
I tend to be like now,

00:41:26.550 --> 00:41:28.210
but I think the way you framed it up,

00:41:28.210 --> 00:41:31.940
I wouldn't mind for you to
actually build the storyline

00:41:31.940 --> 00:41:33.210
because it's that logo

00:41:33.210 --> 00:41:34.610
that's gonna actually deliver

00:41:34.610 --> 00:41:35.930
what you're trying to deliver.

00:41:35.930 --> 00:41:38.740
- [Liam] Yeah, totally, awesome.

00:41:38.740 --> 00:41:40.120
And my second question is

00:41:40.120 --> 00:41:42.750
I just brought a hoodie from
me as well to give to you,

00:41:42.750 --> 00:41:44.221
if you wouldn't mind,

00:41:44.221 --> 00:41:45.280
I'd love to give it to you after.

00:41:45.280 --> 00:41:46.530
- You can give it to me now.

00:41:46.530 --> 00:41:47.590
- [Liam] Sweet, I'll grab it for you.

00:41:47.590 --> 00:41:48.423
Thanks.

00:41:48.423 --> 00:41:49.465
- You got it, bro.

00:41:49.465 --> 00:41:50.420
- [Nathan] How you going, Gary?

00:41:50.420 --> 00:41:51.470
My name's Nathan.

00:41:51.470 --> 00:41:52.420
- Nathan, how are you?

00:41:52.420 --> 00:41:53.779
- [Nathan] Yeah good, thanks.

00:41:53.779 --> 00:41:58.190
You seem pretty chill
and on top of things.

00:41:58.190 --> 00:42:00.050
So my question is

00:42:00.050 --> 00:42:03.440
how do you handle stress and adversity

00:42:03.440 --> 00:42:05.090
in your businesses?

00:42:05.090 --> 00:42:07.223
- By realizing it doesn't mean dick.

00:42:09.180 --> 00:42:10.558
I mean it.

00:42:10.558 --> 00:42:12.420
I have never been able to
really get down on business

00:42:12.420 --> 00:42:15.000
because I basically
make pretend in my mind

00:42:15.000 --> 00:42:17.130
when something awful happens in business

00:42:17.130 --> 00:42:20.970
that instead of this
awful thing that happened,

00:42:20.970 --> 00:42:22.450
we had a great day

00:42:22.450 --> 00:42:23.530
but I got a phone call

00:42:23.530 --> 00:42:26.050
that one of the 10 people
I love the most died

00:42:26.050 --> 00:42:28.440
in a horrific accident

00:42:28.440 --> 00:42:30.870
and it just wakes me up
and puts me in perspec,

00:42:30.870 --> 00:42:33.020
I have business in a very big perspective.

00:42:33.020 --> 00:42:37.320
I am unbelievably not interested in money.

00:42:37.320 --> 00:42:40.230
I do not validate myself,

00:42:40.230 --> 00:42:42.850
I'm not interested in flashy shit.

00:42:42.850 --> 00:42:44.380
I'm into the game.

00:42:44.380 --> 00:42:45.890
Money is great, it's fine,

00:42:45.890 --> 00:42:47.700
it rewards a lot of opportunity

00:42:47.700 --> 00:42:51.570
but the stress is easy

00:42:51.570 --> 00:42:54.080
when you don't have
your emotions wrapped up

00:42:54.080 --> 00:42:56.034
in the success of your business.

00:42:56.034 --> 00:42:57.360
- [Nathan] Yeah.

00:42:57.360 --> 00:43:00.450
- Like I love doing business.

00:43:00.450 --> 00:43:01.760
The reason I garage sale

00:43:01.760 --> 00:43:05.040
or go do a week at a baseball
card show, like I just did,

00:43:05.040 --> 00:43:06.940
is 'cause I love the process,

00:43:06.940 --> 00:43:10.300
not the gifts that are
given to me personally

00:43:10.300 --> 00:43:12.032
from the business.

00:43:12.032 --> 00:43:16.097
So the stress that I get from business

00:43:16.097 --> 00:43:18.690
is extremely low

00:43:18.690 --> 00:43:21.200
because I'm not scared to go to zero.

00:43:21.200 --> 00:43:23.260
- [Nathan] Yeah, makes sense.

00:43:23.260 --> 00:43:24.140
- You understand?

00:43:24.140 --> 00:43:25.509
- [Nathan] Yeah.

00:43:25.509 --> 00:43:26.810
- And that, if you go deeper,

00:43:26.810 --> 00:43:28.510
is grounded in the fact

00:43:28.510 --> 00:43:29.440
that I don't give a fuck

00:43:29.440 --> 00:43:30.890
what anybody thinks about me.

00:43:32.760 --> 00:43:34.370
- [Nathan] Yeah.

00:43:34.370 --> 00:43:35.770
- If I completely collapse

00:43:35.770 --> 00:43:37.770
and go to zero and everybody here

00:43:37.770 --> 00:43:39.820
and all of social and
all of internet says,

00:43:39.820 --> 00:43:41.090
see, he was full of shit,

00:43:41.090 --> 00:43:42.170
he wasn't good,

00:43:42.170 --> 00:43:43.903
I genuinely wouldn't care.

00:43:46.760 --> 00:43:48.530
I just have no interest in living my life

00:43:48.530 --> 00:43:50.180
based on other people's opinions.

00:43:52.114 --> 00:43:54.991
- [Nathan] Thank you.

00:43:54.991 --> 00:43:57.480
- I just think you need to
put business in perspective.

00:43:57.480 --> 00:43:59.623
And also, I'm thankful for playing.

00:44:00.890 --> 00:44:03.620
The cost of entry of being an entrepreneur

00:44:03.620 --> 00:44:06.023
is having ridiculously difficult days.

00:44:06.920 --> 00:44:09.729
You want to live your
life on your own terms,

00:44:09.729 --> 00:44:12.220
of course it should be hard,

00:44:12.220 --> 00:44:13.770
otherwise we'd all be doing it.

00:44:15.214 --> 00:44:16.900
Perspective.

00:44:16.900 --> 00:44:18.266
- [Nathan] Thanks.

00:44:18.266 --> 00:44:19.388
- You got it.

00:44:19.388 --> 00:44:20.600
- [Samara] Hi Gary.

00:44:20.600 --> 00:44:21.433
- Hey.

00:44:21.433 --> 00:44:22.905
- [Samara] My name's Samara.

00:44:22.905 --> 00:44:23.750
I work for digital media company

00:44:23.750 --> 00:44:25.760
called Fish Eye Creative in New Castle.

00:44:25.760 --> 00:44:26.820
My question is,

00:44:26.820 --> 00:44:28.230
so I have no interest

00:44:28.230 --> 00:44:30.770
in being the business
owner or the entrepreneur.

00:44:30.770 --> 00:44:32.950
I want to be the best number two.

00:44:32.950 --> 00:44:34.400
- I love that.

00:44:34.400 --> 00:44:35.910
- [Samara] And I would like to know

00:44:35.910 --> 00:44:39.070
what you would say to your number two,

00:44:39.070 --> 00:44:41.680
what's the best way to
add to the productivity

00:44:41.680 --> 00:44:43.390
and the value of the company

00:44:43.390 --> 00:44:45.110
and to assist the number one?

00:44:45.110 --> 00:44:48.150
- By reverse engineering the
number one's shortcomings.

00:44:48.150 --> 00:44:49.230
- [Samara] Sorry?

00:44:49.230 --> 00:44:50.370
- By reverse engineering

00:44:50.370 --> 00:44:52.540
the number one's shortcomings.

00:44:52.540 --> 00:44:53.373
- [Samara] Okay.

00:44:53.373 --> 00:44:55.490
- The best thing a number two can do

00:44:55.490 --> 00:44:57.977
is close the gaps of a number one.

00:44:57.977 --> 00:44:59.920
- [Samara] Cool.

00:44:59.920 --> 00:45:01.510
- Are you a good match to your number one?

00:45:01.510 --> 00:45:02.343
- [Samara] Yes.

00:45:02.343 --> 00:45:03.986
- Well then that's a good starting point.

00:45:03.986 --> 00:45:04.819
- [Samara] Awesome.

00:45:04.819 --> 00:45:05.940
Thank you.

00:45:05.940 --> 00:45:08.950
- To me, it's about complementary
skills at that level

00:45:08.950 --> 00:45:11.810
and so it's just,

00:45:11.810 --> 00:45:13.550
a lot of times, number two's struggle

00:45:13.550 --> 00:45:14.900
because they want to do

00:45:14.900 --> 00:45:17.660
or they're equally have the same talents

00:45:17.660 --> 00:45:18.580
as the number one

00:45:18.580 --> 00:45:20.490
and that's where friction comes from.

00:45:20.490 --> 00:45:22.950
I think it's a game of
complementary skills.

00:45:22.950 --> 00:45:25.780
And so the relationships that I've seen

00:45:25.780 --> 00:45:26.980
and the ones that have worked for me

00:45:26.980 --> 00:45:28.620
is when the number two

00:45:28.620 --> 00:45:31.810
is filling in the blanks of the number one

00:45:31.810 --> 00:45:33.250
and allowing the number one

00:45:33.250 --> 00:45:35.750
to do her or his magic.

00:45:35.750 --> 00:45:36.583
- Thank you.

00:45:36.583 --> 00:45:37.490
- You're welcome.
- I really appreciate

00:45:37.490 --> 00:45:38.740
you validating that it's okay

00:45:38.740 --> 00:45:40.710
not to be the entrepreneur as well.

00:45:40.710 --> 00:45:41.600
I appreciate that.

00:45:41.600 --> 00:45:42.433
- Yeah.

00:45:42.433 --> 00:45:46.950
My great fear is that as
entrepreneurship has gotten popular

00:45:46.950 --> 00:45:50.300
obviously that's been
directly a benefit to me

00:45:50.300 --> 00:45:51.840
but I have no interest

00:45:51.840 --> 00:45:55.110
in anybody aspiring to
be one when they're not

00:45:55.110 --> 00:45:57.090
in the same way that I take a lot of issue

00:45:57.090 --> 00:45:59.550
with people thinking
that going to university

00:45:59.550 --> 00:46:00.927
is the way to go.

00:46:00.927 --> 00:46:04.640
We have to change the conversation

00:46:04.640 --> 00:46:07.580
and make this about
happiness and self awareness,

00:46:07.580 --> 00:46:10.187
not fucking money.

00:46:10.187 --> 00:46:11.793
- [Samara] Yeah, thank you.

00:46:16.020 --> 00:46:16.853
- [Ami] Hi Gary.

00:46:16.853 --> 00:46:18.460
It's Ami Mishel from Sydney.

00:46:18.460 --> 00:46:20.101
- How are you?

00:46:20.101 --> 00:46:21.098
- [Ami] Fantastic, thank you.

00:46:21.098 --> 00:46:22.117
How are you?

00:46:22.117 --> 00:46:23.115
- Really, really good.

00:46:23.115 --> 00:46:25.101
- [Ami] I've got a hashtag
question for you, Gary.

00:46:25.101 --> 00:46:27.710
We develop residential property

00:46:27.710 --> 00:46:30.500
in a regional town called
Oberon, New South Wales.

00:46:30.500 --> 00:46:31.333
- Okay.

00:46:32.167 --> 00:46:33.620
- [Ami] And if the hashtag
oberonnewsouthwales

00:46:33.620 --> 00:46:34.980
isn't popular yet,

00:46:34.980 --> 00:46:37.540
what do you do to grow a hashtag

00:46:37.540 --> 00:46:39.640
that people wouldn't search for it

00:46:39.640 --> 00:46:41.310
unless they knew about it?

00:46:41.310 --> 00:46:43.520
- Why would you want it to be popular?

00:46:43.520 --> 00:46:46.360
- [Ami] Well I'd want people
to see a small regional town

00:46:46.360 --> 00:46:48.440
of 3,600 people

00:46:48.440 --> 00:46:50.860
getting $200 million into it

00:46:50.860 --> 00:46:54.820
as popular despite it's size.

00:46:54.820 --> 00:46:56.370
- But why would you do that in the form

00:46:56.370 --> 00:46:58.820
of making a hashtag popular?

00:46:58.820 --> 00:47:01.550
- [Ami] Well, I'm more into
people finding the town

00:47:01.550 --> 00:47:02.750
and organically looking

00:47:02.750 --> 00:47:06.610
at why they should invest money
in my project in that town.

00:47:06.610 --> 00:47:08.720
- Well you should do that
by putting out content

00:47:08.720 --> 00:47:09.690
to build awareness.

00:47:09.690 --> 00:47:12.040
Because a hashtag is not
gonna do that for you.

00:47:14.360 --> 00:47:15.720
- [Ami] So content specific for the town

00:47:15.720 --> 00:47:17.780
or content of developments

00:47:17.780 --> 00:47:19.760
or why you should invest in general?

00:47:19.760 --> 00:47:21.020
- Yes.

00:47:21.020 --> 00:47:21.853
- [Ami] General?

00:47:21.853 --> 00:47:22.686
- Both.

00:47:23.880 --> 00:47:26.510
A hashtag is a tactic

00:47:26.510 --> 00:47:28.053
that isn't ownable.

00:47:28.930 --> 00:47:30.520
I can put out a post right now

00:47:30.520 --> 00:47:32.480
of why people should invest in soccer

00:47:32.480 --> 00:47:33.950
and proper football cards

00:47:33.950 --> 00:47:36.160
and put that hashtag in my post.

00:47:36.160 --> 00:47:38.490
Hashtags are not ownable.

00:47:38.490 --> 00:47:39.900
And they're not the discovery tool

00:47:39.900 --> 00:47:41.303
that you assume they are.

00:47:42.190 --> 00:47:44.440
You should run creative

00:47:44.440 --> 00:47:49.420
in the form of videos and
probably white papers and decks

00:47:49.420 --> 00:47:50.570
and then you should target them

00:47:50.570 --> 00:47:52.383
against development investors.

00:47:54.580 --> 00:47:56.310
- [Ami] So target the white papers

00:47:56.310 --> 00:47:59.587
with the content and then--

00:47:59.587 --> 00:48:00.790
- And target the people,

00:48:00.790 --> 00:48:02.770
